# Flyway migration version ranges

When creating a new `V*__*.sql` under `src/main/resources/db/migration/`:

| Developer | Allowed versions |
|-----------|------------------|
| Abdul Moid | 100–349 |
| Nameera | 350–599 |
| Humaid | 600–849 |
| Abdul Mannan | 850–1099 |

## Rules

- Use the next free integer **inside your own range** (scan existing files in `db/migration/` first).
- Never use V1–V99 for new work (reserved / already used history on `main`).
- Never edit a migration after it is on `main`; add a new migration instead.
- Ask which developer you are if unclear; do not guess another person's range.
- Example: Abdul Moid's next migration after `V100__foo.sql` is `V101__bar.sql`.
